nning."]}, "overview": "Sarah Huckabee Sanders seeks a second term as governor in a state that leans Republican by about fifteen points. Her Democratic challenger, Fredrick Love, has run a low-profile campaign with little visible fundraising, and a Libertarian candidate also appears on the ballot. Seven raters across the spectrum place the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Love roughly a three percent chance of winning.\n\nThe one public poll, a Hendrix College survey of likely voters from August, showed Sanders ahead by five points, closer than the state's usual margins, amid headlines about waning approval. A September campaign ad on Medicaid work requirements drew criticism from the NAACP and some conservative commentators, but no follow-up polling has appeared. Incumbency, state lean, and market pricing make Sanders a strong favorite, with remaining uncertainty tied to her softened standing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -11.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0294, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.026, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0419, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0317, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0391, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -1